    "gp_section_550122344216265925": {
      "settings": {
        "checksum": "b64d0812b04bc7d4ad1d88beff21d81fd4cc3679b31909989b99291f1099b3c8_1_1_0_0__1",
        "gCLdyyCXYoDSn_text": "<strong>What Is Shilajit?</strong>",
        "gDJblOJxcKbOE_text": "Increase Collagen Synthesis",
        "gFxyHcjCtxcDt_text": "Increase Strength",
        "gGsBdFFGBlWmW_text": "TOP 5 SHOPPING MISTAKES",
        "gLDSSkMrKvIUY_text": "Sourcing Matters: Beware of Shilajit not sourced from high-altitude regions like the Himalayas. Shilajit from lower altitude regions lacks purity and potency",
        "gLSvWVLPFBaAr_text": "<strong>Doses &amp; Side Effects</strong>",
        "gMujuoVohcjQE_text": "<p>Low Fulvic Acid: Watch for products with low fulvic acid content (below 70%). Products with low fulvic acid ratios won't provide optimal benefits.</p>",
        "gNOqGaKWEVvhF_text": "<p>Shilajit is a sticky, dark, resinous substance found predominantly in the mountainous regions of the Himalayas. This compound is traditionally used in Indian medicine due to its dense mineral content and ability to heal.</p>",
        "gNqnMsLyMxBdL_text": "<p>If you feel mentally and physically drained, and it only seems to get worse with time, we have a treat for you...</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>See, our Western diet lacks essential nutrients and minerals, which leads to widespread chronic health decline.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This nutritional deficiency manifests in symptoms like brittle joints and bones, muscular weakness, low energy, and accelerated aging.<br><br>You've tried everything, and nothing seems to help. Why? Because it all starts with minerals...minerals you aren't getting in western foods.<br><br><strong><u>Shilajit provides a hyper-concentrated supply of 84 of 102 minerals that are essential for filling in these nutrient gaps.</u></strong></p>",
        "gOqpwUiqUBfXW_text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:32px;\"><strong>Why Do We Need Shilajit?</strong></span></p>",
        "gPBIgnzkeIVHn_text": "Increases Bone Density",
        "gPZyrPPAQzsUF_text": "<p>Cheap Shilajit: Shilajit isn't cheap, even in India. AMzN is filled with garbage. These brands drop-ship \"shilajit\" straight from China to your door. Don't buy anything under $30- it's not real.*</p>",
        "gRPPjmtjNHpGn_text": "<p>SIow Down Aging</p>",
        "gSwQScGxVHdUb_text": "<p>When choosing shilajit, prioritize quality and safety. Look for brands with lab reports showing high Fulvic Acid and no heavy metals. Choose easy-to-use forms. High-quality shilajit is often dark, sticky, and has an earthy smell. Always rely on lab reports for the most accurate assessment.</p>",
        "gTWopkFhNlVMB_text": "Lack of Lab Testing: Don't buy from brands that don't test for heavy metals, contaminants, and salmonella. Since it's an organic material, you want it to be tested..",
        "gUBPZBMzfnAvA_text": "Energy & Endurance",
        "gUJvTWTutWMbz_text": "Optimize Hormone Levels",
        "gVFWKrJSvwMai_text": "A QUALITY SHILAJIT SUPPLEMENT CAN",
        "gWQamTyJaiZIn_text": "<p><strong>Quality Matters in Gummies &amp; Supplements</strong></p>",
        "ggOJ0HnHxqc_text": "<p><strong>Caplets:</strong> Shilajit caps provide a convenient and tasteless way to consume it. They can be more potent than the resin, assuming the brand is using a quality extract.</p>",
        "ggR6PjDBjvz_text": "<p><strong>Grade and Effectiveness:</strong> May be lower grade and less effective due to processing and lower-quality sourcing.</p>",
        "ggYNaVI0EY3_text": "<p><strong>Gummies:</strong> Ease of use and controlled dosage makes gummies ideal for daily consumption...but only if you can find one that tastes great.</p>",
        "ggayTO6TPwj_text": "<p><strong>Extract: </strong>Shilajit extract is a more potent form of resin that's been dehydrated, typically used in caplets and gummies. There are varying degrees of potency depending on the ratio. A 30:1 ratio is 3x's stronger than 10:1, for example.</p>",
        "ggirBNt77qf_text": "<p><strong>Sourcing:</strong> Typically sourced from lower elevations, potentially impacting quality and potency.</p>",
        "ggqQ5fWFh4N_text": "<p><strong>THE DIFFERENT FORMS OF SHILAJIT</strong></p>",
        "giKpnStDcSLRy_text": "<p>The recommended dosage depends on several factors, including age and if it's a resin or extract.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The internet recommends 250-500mg of resin per day...<strong>but that's not accurate, nor scientific - and the resin is impossible to measure. For this reason, I would avoid resin all together.</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Only buy an extract!</p><p><br>The main thing you are looking for is a 50% fulvic acid ratio, which tells you how nutrient dense the extract is.</p>",
        "goBuOZmeRZJUC_text": "<strong>Benefits For Men &amp; Women</strong>",
        "grqEXPgCtpeHH_text": "<p><strong>Low Shilajit Potency</strong>: Contains&nbsp;10-20% fulvic acid</p>",
        "gtext-row-i2l4c577ed6f4-1_text": "<p><strong>Flavoring:</strong> Often flavored with added sugars and artificial flavors.</p>",
        "gtext-row-i2l4c577ed6f4-2_text": "<p><strong>Absorption:</strong> Processing may reduce the absorption of beneficial compounds.</p>",
        "gufyPityYGUvN_text": "<p><strong>Resin: </strong>Shilajit resin is the traditional form. It's not as concentrated or potent as the extracts, and requires you to eat it raw or mix into tea.</p>",
        "gwJHcCqBEjSJN_text": "<p>Shilajit contains fulvic acid, a compound critical for absorbing minerals, detoxification, and antioxidant effects.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Shilajit contains two unique molecules that aren't found anywhere else in nature. These fascinating compounds contribute to its diverse effects and anti-inflammatory properties, potentially slowing the aging process.</p>",
        "gytBzFzxYdrhk_text": "<p><strong>HOT TIP</strong></p>"
      },
      "type": "gp-section-550122344216265925"
    },
